    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T17:26:48Z",
    "body": "feat on infield:issue/728-altmill · PR #733 (draft, stacked on #715) · pinned by altmill_machines::{every_altmill_states_its_figures, every_tool_change_lifts_to_the_homed_top_then_stands_alone, a_spindle_speed_past_the_maximum_is_refused, the_4x4_two_tool_program_is_locked} and machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration · merges at the next cut (fork synced at v0.16.0)\n\nTwo things differ from the issue text above:\n- **No ATC or manual mode, and no rack list.** gSender and ncSender both take over on `T<n> M6`, so the grblHAL post's plain `T<n> M6` serves manual changes, RapidChange and Sienci's ATC alike. Which tools are in the rack is left to the sender and the ATC.\n- **Corrected figures.** From Sienci's spec pages: the 4x8 is 1265 x 2460 x 210 mm (not Y 2640), and the 2x4/4x4 Z is 174 mm. The 4x4 uses the controller's soft limits (1260 x 1248 x 170 mm).\n\nDetails in `docs/decisions/728-altmill.md`. Labels needed (I can't set them from outside): `in-review` in place of the claim.\n",
